The error Cannot DELETE /deleteAccount usually means your Express app doesn't have a route that matches the request being made. There are also a few issues in the route you've posted.

1. Your route expects a URL parameter

You defined:

app.delete("/deleteAccount/:id", async (req, res) => {

So the request must look like:

DELETE /deleteAccount/64f8c1...

If you're sending:

DELETE /deleteAccount

Express won't find a matching route, resulting in:

Cannot DELETE /deleteAccount
2. Use req.params.id, not req.query._id

Since your route uses :id, retrieve it like this:

const { id } = req.params;

not

req.query._id
3. Typo in findByIdAndDelete

You have:

account.finByIdAndDelete(...)

It should be:

Account.findByIdAndDelete(...)

assuming your Mongoose model is called Account.

4. You're using account for two different things

Avoid this:

const account = await account.findByIdAndDelete(...);

Instead:

const deletedAccount = await Account.findByIdAndDelete(id);
5. error doesn't exist in your 404 block

You have:

return res.status(404).send({
    message: "account not found",
    code: error.code,
    stack: error.stack,
});

There is no error there. Just return:

return res.status(404).json({
    message: "Account not found",
});
Correct version
app.delete("/deleteAccount/:id", async (req, res) => {
    try {
        const { id } = req.params;

        const deletedAccount = await Account.findByIdAndDelete(id);

        if (!deletedAccount) {
            return res.status(404).json({
                message: "Account not found",
            });
        }

        res.status(200).json({
            message: "Account deleted successfully",
            deletedAccount,
        });
    } catch (error) {
        res.status(500).json({
            message: error.message,
        });
    }
});
