That's completely fine. If the rest of your API uses query parameters, it's reasonable to keep it consistent.

In that case, your route should look like this:

app.delete("/deleteAccount", async (req, res) => {
    try {
        const { _id } = req.query;

        const result = await db
            .collection("acounts")
            .deleteOne({ _id: new ObjectId(_id) });

        if (result.deletedCount === 0) {
            return res.status(404).json({
                message: "Account not found",
            });
        }

        res.status(200).json({
            message: "Account deleted successfully",
        });
    } catch (error) {
        res.status(500).json({
            message: error.message,
        });
    }
});

And your Postman URL:

DELETE https://easy-animals.onrender.com/deleteAccount?_id=6a6622d3dac250f60c4f76f3

matches that route.

